# The Spanish phrasebook: every phrase the language lessons name, by key, in Castilian as it is
# spoken in Spain. A typed answer in a box written accents=loose may leave the acute accent and the
# diaeresis off; ñ is a letter of its own and is always marked.
phrasebook es v=1 lenient=[acute, diaeresis] {
  name "Spanish"
  variety "Castilian, as spoken in Spain"
  entry ability.can-you-dance "¿Sabes bailar?" gloss="Can you dance?"
  entry ability.can-you-sing "¿Sabes cantar?" gloss="Can you sing?"
